SCALAR_COSINE_GEOMETRY_INSUFFICIENT

Exact online local cosine matching does not reproduce the locked semantic transport profile. AkbasCore 3.0 should retain DRA as the actuator but should NOT use scalar cosine/alignment as the sole controller state. The controller needs richer local directional/subspace/manifold state.


INTERPRETATION LOCK
-------------------

BRANCH A
========

IF semantic A and B D19 values are reproduced by their corresponding
ONLINE geometry-matched random nulls:

    TEST113's semantic/random difference is substantially explained by
    local hidden-state alignment.

    MOTOR CONSEQUENCE:

        AkbasCore 3.0 can prioritize:

            hidden state
                 ↓
            geometric state estimator
                 ↓
            G_l(state)
                 ↓
            DRA actuator

        without concept-specific semantic labels as the primary
        controller variable.


BRANCH B
========

IF semantic A and B D19 remain above all corresponding matched controls:

    Matching scalar cosine at the actual intervention point is not enough.

    MOTOR CONSEQUENCE:

        G_l = f(cosine)

    is insufficient.

    AkbasCore 3.0 should instead represent richer local state such as:

        directional subspace position
        manifold relationship
        local directional coherence
        layerwise transport state

    while DRA remains the actuator.


MIXED BRANCH
============

IF A and B split:

    one scalar geometric law does not explain both directions.

    Preserve directional asymmetry in the AkbasCore 3.0 state model.


IMPORTANT
=========

A residual difference does NOT prove that "semantics" itself is causal.

It only rejects the tested scalar local-cosine explanation.

No controller has been trained here.
No parameter has been tuned from the outcome.
No feature has been selected post-hoc.

